<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Würm (Nagold)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Würm is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a> that rises south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a> and flows north-west through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weil-der-stadt">Weil der Stadt</a> to join the Nagold at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pforzheim">Pforzheim</a>. Its valley crosses the Heckengäu, a limestone plateau west of Stuttgart, and several small medieval towns grew along its banks, among them the free imperial city of Weil der Stadt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wurm-nagold.jpg" alt="Würm (Nagold)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joachim Moskalewski · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wuerm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
